2.43.m:
Having granted him an auspicious boon, the goddess went to heaven.
The great king returned to his own home with a joyful heart;
having arrived, he related the events concerning his son.

2.44.m:
thirdly, the auspicious one was worshipped by King Maṅgala;
fourthly, she was worshipped by beautiful women on Tuesday;
fifthly, Maṅgalacaṇḍikā [was worshipped] by men desiring auspiciousness. // 38

